### ==============================================================================
### STEP 1: Authentication Endpoints
### ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Login as ADMIN to get fresh token (Optional)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@drivevue.com",
  "password": "adminpassword123"
}

###

### 1.2 Register regular USER (For testing role protection)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Standard User",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "user123456",
  "role": "USER"
}

###

### 1.3 Login as regular USER (To obtain non-admin token)
# @name userLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "user123456"
}

@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.token}}

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 2: Car Management - Create Car (ADMIN Only, Protected Route)
### ==============================================================================

### 2.1 Add Electric Car (Tesla Model 3 Performance) - FULLY VALID PAYLOAD
# @name createTesla
POST {{baseUrl}}/cars
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Tesla Model 3 Performance",
  "brand": "Tesla",
  "model": "Model 3",
  "year": 2024,
  "pricePerDay": 120,
  "category": "Electric",
  "fuelType": "Electric",
  "transmission": "Automatic",
  "seats": 5,
  "images": [
    "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1560958089-b8a1929cea89?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
    "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1536700503339-1e4b06520771?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80"
  ],
  "isAvailable": true
}

### Capture created car ID for use in subsequent GET, PATCH, and DELETE requests
@carId = {{createTesla.response.body.data._id}}

###

