### ==============================================================================
### STEP 3: Car Management - Read & Filter Cars (Public Routes)
### ==============================================================================

### 3.1 Get All Cars (No filters applied)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars

###

### 3.2 Filter Cars by Brand (e.g. Tesla)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars?brand=Tesla

###

### 3.3 Filter Cars by Category (Allowed: Sedan, SUV, Luxury, Electric, Sports)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars?category=SUV

###

### 3.4 Filter Cars by Fuel Type (Allowed: Petrol, Diesel, Hybrid, Electric)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars?fuelType=Electric

###

### 3.5 Search Cars by Keyword (Searches name, brand, or model)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars?search=Tesla

###

### 3.6 Combined Filters and Search Query
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars?category=Electric&fuelType=Electric&search=Model

###

### 3.7 Filter Cars by Availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars?isAvailable=true

###

### 3.8 Get Single Car Details by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars/{{carId}}

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 4: Car Management - Update Car (ADMIN Only)
### ==============================================================================

### 4.1 Update Car Price and Availability via PATCH
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/cars/{{carId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "pricePerDay": 135,
  "isAvailable": false
}

###

### 4.2 Update Car via PUT
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cars/{{carId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "pricePerDay": 140,
  "isAvailable": true
}

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 5: Car Management - Delete Car (ADMIN Only)
### ==============================================================================

### 5.1 Delete Car by ID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cars/{{carId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###

### 5.2 Verify Deletion (Should return 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars/{{carId}}

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 6: Validation & Error Handling Tests (Debug Demonstrations)
### ==============================================================================

### 6.1 Test Missing Required Fields (Should return detailed 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cars
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Incomplete Car"
}

###

### 6.2 Test Invalid Field Types (Should return detailed 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cars
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Invalid Type Car",
  "brand": "Tesla",
  "model": "Model Y",
  "year": "not_a_number",
  "pricePerDay": -50,
  "category": "FlyingCar",
  "fuelType": "Kerosene",
  "seats": 0
}

###

### 6.3 Test Unauthorized Request (Missing Token -> 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cars
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Unauthenticated Car",
  "brand": "Toyota",
  "model": "Camry",
  "year": 2023,
  "pricePerDay": 70,
  "category": "Sedan",
  "fuelType": "Petrol",
  "seats": 5
}

###

### 6.4 Test Forbidden Request (Regular User Token -> 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cars
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "name": "Forbidden Car",
  "brand": "Toyota",
  "model": "Camry",
  "year": 2023,
  "pricePerDay": 70,
  "category": "Sedan",
  "fuelType": "Petrol",
  "seats": 5
}
